{"book":19,"chapter":11,"rubric":"LINUX NETWORKING / CHAPTER 11","slides":[{"title":"Why bond, MTU and ethtool","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"Why","main":"One cable, one failure; bond, ethtool and MTU close the gaps.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Cable","Bond","ethtool","MTU"],"captions":["One cable is one point of failure and one speed ceiling","The bonding driver joins interfaces into one logical interface","ethtool shows what happens to the card: link, counters, offloads","The MTU decides which frames fit the path; team is removed in RHEL 10"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"one cable = one failure","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"one cable = one failure","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"bond: cards as one","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"one cable = one failure","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"bond: cards as one","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ethtool: what the card sees","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"one cable = one failure","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"bond: cards as one","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ethtool: what the card sees","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"MTU: which frame fits","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[9.0,19.1,29.5]}]},{"title":"Seven bond modes","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"Modes","main":"Modes 0-6: round, backup, by hash, to all, adaptive.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["0 and 3","1","2 and 4","5 and 6"],"captions":["balance-rr in turn (default) and broadcast on all interfaces","active-backup: one works, the others wait","balance-xor and 802.3ad pick an interface by the flow hash","balance-tlb and balance-alb need no switch setup (like mode 1)"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"0 rr, 3 broadcast: round / all","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"0 rr, 3 broadcast: round / all","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1 active-backup: one active","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"0 rr, 3 broadcast: round / all","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1 active-backup: one active","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2 xor, 4 802.3ad: by hash","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"0 rr, 3 broadcast: round / all","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"1 active-backup: one active","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"2 xor, 4 802.3ad: by hash","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"5 tlb, 6 alb: self-balancing","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[10.6,17.8,28.0]}]},{"title":"Creating a bond","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"Create","main":"ip link add type bond; bring slaves down and set master.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["bond","eth0","eth1","up"],"captions":["A bond is a device of type bond: mode, miimon, hash policy","Bring the card down, then set master; the kernel refuses an up card","Same for the second card; its MTU becomes the bond's MTU","Bring the bond up and check the result with ip -d link"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["ip link add bond0 type bond \\","   mode 802.3ad miimon 100 \\","   xmit_hash_policy layer3+4","ip link set eth0 down","ip link set eth0 master bond0","ip link set eth1 down","ip link set eth1 master bond0","ip link set bond0 up","ip -d link show bond0"],"hl":[0,1,2],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["ip link add bond0 type bond \\","   mode 802.3ad miimon 100 \\","   xmit_hash_policy layer3+4","ip link set eth0 down","ip link set eth0 master bond0","ip link set eth1 down","ip link set eth1 master bond0","ip link set bond0 up","ip -d link show bond0"],"hl":[3,4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["ip link add bond0 type bond \\","   mode 802.3ad miimon 100 \\","   xmit_hash_policy layer3+4","ip link set eth0 down","ip link set eth0 master bond0","ip link set eth1 down","ip link set eth1 master bond0","ip link set bond0 up","ip -d link show bond0"],"hl":[5,6],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["ip link add bond0 type bond \\","   mode 802.3ad miimon 100 \\","   xmit_hash_policy layer3+4","ip link set eth0 down","ip link set eth0 master bond0","ip link set eth1 down","ip link set eth1 master bond0","ip link set bond0 up","ip -d link show bond0"],"hl":[7,8],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[8.6,18.5,26.8]}]},{"title":"/proc/net/bonding/bond0","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"proc","main":"The bond header and one block per enslaved interface.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Mode","Polling","Slave","Failures"],"captions":["Header: the mode and the active interface","The polling period and delays are printed in milliseconds","A slave block: status up, going down, down or going back","Link Failure Count grows for a flapping cable or port"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["Bonding Mode: fault-tolerance (active-backup)","Currently Active Slave: eth0","MII Polling Interval (ms): 100","Down Delay (ms): 200","Slave Interface: eth1","MII Status: going down","Link Failure Count: 3"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["Bonding Mode: fault-tolerance (active-backup)","Currently Active Slave: eth0","MII Polling Interval (ms): 100","Down Delay (ms): 200","Slave Interface: eth1","MII Status: going down","Link Failure Count: 3"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["Bonding Mode: fault-tolerance (active-backup)","Currently Active Slave: eth0","MII Polling Interval (ms): 100","Down Delay (ms): 200","Slave Interface: eth1","MII Status: going down","Link Failure Count: 3"],"hl":[4,5],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["Bonding Mode: fault-tolerance (active-backup)","Currently Active Slave: eth0","MII Polling Interval (ms): 100","Down Delay (ms): 200","Slave Interface: eth1","MII Status: going down","Link Failure Count: 3"],"hl":[6],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[8.3,19.8,31.1]}]},{"title":"Link check: miimon","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"miimon","main":"Four slave states and two delays.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["up","going down","down","going back"],"captions":["Every miimon ms the driver checks the carrier; 0 disables polling","Carrier lost: going down, downdelay is counted","Not back: down, the bond takes the interface out of work","Back: going back, updelay is counted; both are multiples of miimon"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":46.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"up\nlink ok","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":46.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"up\nlink ok","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":135.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"going down\nwait delay","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a1","x1":85.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":96.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":46.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"up\nlink ok","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":135.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"going down\nwait delay","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a1","x1":85.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":96.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":224.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"down\nfailed","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a2","x1":174.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":185.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":46.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"up\nlink ok","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":135.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"going down\nwait delay","tone":"yellow","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a1","x1":85.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":96.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":224.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"down\nfailed","tone":"red","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a2","x1":174.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":185.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"red","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":313.0,"y":70.0,"w":76.0,"h":52.0,"text":"going back\nwait delay","tone":"blue","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"a3","x1":263.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":274.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[11.6,19.8,29.8]}]},{"title":"Hash and xmit_hash_policy","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"Hash","main":"layer2, layer2+3, layer3+4: more fields, wider spread.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["layer2","layer2+3","layer3+4","Result"],"captions":["layer2: last MAC bytes and protocol type, a peer stays on one interface","layer2+3: IP addresses are added","layer3+4: ports are added, TCP connections spread out","hash mod N gives the index; one connection never leaves its interface"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"layer2: MAC[5] ^ MAC[5] ^ type","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"layer2: MAC[5] ^ MAC[5] ^ type","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"layer2+3: + IP addresses","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"layer2: MAC[5] ^ MAC[5] ^ type","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"layer2+3: + IP addresses","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"layer3+4: ports ^ IP, >>1","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"layer2: MAC[5] ^ MAC[5] ^ type","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"layer2+3: + IP addresses","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"layer3+4: ports ^ IP, >>1","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"hash mod N = slave index","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[12.4,18.0,27.2]}]},{"title":"LACP and aggregators","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"LACP","main":"Both sides agree on the aggregator members.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Ports","LACPDU","Aggregator","Failure"],"captions":["On the switch the ports are put into a LACP channel","Both sides send LACPDUs: fast every 1 s, slow every 30 s","Ports of equal speed and duplex form one aggregator","Another Aggregator ID or a zero partner MAC: no agreement"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"switch:\nports in LACP","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"switch:\nports in LACP","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":265.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"LACPDU\n1 s / 30 s","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"switch:\nports in LACP","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":265.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"LACPDU\n1 s / 30 s","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":95.0,"y":110.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"one aggregator,\none speed","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"switch:\nports in LACP","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":265.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"LACPDU\n1 s / 30 s","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":95.0,"y":110.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"one aggregator,\none speed","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":265.0,"y":110.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"other ID or\npartner MAC 0","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[9.1,19.1,28.1]}]},{"title":"ethtool: link, counters, offloads","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"ethtool","main":"One tool for link, counters, offloads and rings.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Link","Counters","Offloads","Rings"],"captions":["ethtool eth0: Speed, Duplex, Link detected","-S: driver counters; the names differ by vendor","-k shows offloads, [fixed] cannot be changed; -K changes","-g shows the sizes of the rx and tx rings"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["ethtool eth0","ethtool -S eth0","ethtool -k eth0","ethtool -K eth0 gro off tso off","ethtool -g eth0"],"hl":[0],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["ethtool eth0","ethtool -S eth0","ethtool -k eth0","ethtool -K eth0 gro off tso off","ethtool -g eth0"],"hl":[1],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["ethtool eth0","ethtool -S eth0","ethtool -k eth0","ethtool -K eth0 gro off tso off","ethtool -g eth0"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":20.0,"y":24.0,"lines":["ethtool eth0","ethtool -S eth0","ethtool -k eth0","ethtool -K eth0 gro off tso off","ethtool -g eth0"],"hl":[4],"lang":"plain","size":9.0,"lh":13.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[8.4,17.8,29.1]}]},{"title":"MTU and overhead","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"MTU","main":"1500, jumbo 9000, VLAN +4 to the frame, VXLAN minus 50.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Ethernet","VLAN","VXLAN","ping"],"captions":["Ethernet: MTU 1500; jumbo 9000 only if set everywhere","VLAN: +4 bytes to the frame, not to MTU; VLAN MTU is at most the parent's","VXLAN: minus 50 bytes over IPv4, minus 70 over IPv6","Check: ping -M do -s MTU-28, at 1500 that is 1472"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Ethernet: 1500, jumbo 9000","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Ethernet: 1500, jumbo 9000","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"VLAN: +4 to frame, MTU unchanged","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Ethernet: 1500, jumbo 9000","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"VLAN: +4 to frame, MTU unchanged","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"VXLAN: -50 (IPv4), -70 (IPv6)","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Ethernet: 1500, jumbo 9000","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"VLAN: +4 to frame, MTU unchanged","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"VXLAN: -50 (IPv4), -70 (IPv6)","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ping -M do -s MTU-28","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[7.8,18.5,26.0]}]},{"title":"Diagnosing MTU","sub":"Chapter 11 · Linux networking","short":"Diagnosis","main":"Small packets pass, large ones hang: find the limit with ping.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Symptom","Search","Local","Router"],"captions":["Symptom: ping and ssh work, a big file or page hangs","Find the limit: ping -M do -s N, varying N","message too long: the interface's own MTU is too small","Frag needed and DF set (mtu = N): a router on the path replied"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ping works, big file hangs","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ping works, big file hangs","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ping -M do -s 1472 host","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ping works, big file hangs","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ping -M do -s 1472 host","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"local error: message too long","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ping works, big file hangs","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"ping -M do -s 1472 host","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"local error: message too long","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"Frag needed and DF set (mtu=N)","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[9.8,17.7,27.9]}]}]}